1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Ten STL designs. Two mounting options.
Fourteen prints with motor clamps; ten with motor ties. One-piece board platform and combined shoulder/neck.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:13,000
01 | Round reinforced base
Mate four Adafruit 3777 motors with 3766 wheels; lower the pairs into the one-piece base.

3
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:19,000
02 | Four motor screws, or ties
Use four identical printed hook clamps and one M3 screw per motor. Alternative: omit the clamps and use two longitudinal ties per motor.

4
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:25,000
03 | Choose one battery
Retain the Bioenno6Ah LiFePO4 pack, or use the specified12V7Ah or14Ah SLA case. Secure one pack with two padded zip-tie loops.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:36,000
04 | One printed board platform
Fit boards on the bench. Lower the single platform with its four legs over the battery. Secure the feet with screws or ties; keep terminal boots and wiring clear.

6
00:00:36,000 --> 00:00:41,000
05 | Lower the skirt around the base
The whole213mm skirt lowers around the completed base assembly. Four M4 screws engage retained nuts. Lift the skirt for battery service.

7
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:51,000
06 | Bearings in the combined shell
Shoulder and neck are one186mm print. Fit the lower608 bearing and retainers through the open bottom, then the spacer, upper bearing, shims and spindle.

8
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:57,000
07 | Smaller concealed arm boxes
Feed the arms and servo carriers through the open bottom before fitting the speaker. Retain servo cases with M2 screws or ties. Horn screws remain required.

9
00:00:57,000 --> 00:01:04,000
08 | Integrated adjustable head drive
Fit the motor and wheel on the sliding carriage. Lower them from above. Fit the underside nuts while the shell is open, then retract the tyre.

10
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:13,000
09 | Fit controls and seat the shell
Fit the speaker, rear T-Display and switches after internal assembly. Connect labelled plugs, then lower and fasten the complete shoulder and neck.

11
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:20,000
10 | Seat and retain the head
Keep the tyre retracted. Lower the head over the spindle, fit its washer and retaining nut, and verify free rotation.

12
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:29,000
11 | Adjust and lock contact
Seat and retain the head. Turn the adjustment screw to establish light tyre contact, then lock the carriage. Check a full revolution by hand.

13
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:36,000
12 | Local Wi-Fi control
Illustrative rear screen: direct access point, then access point plus a 2.4 GHz network.

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:44,000
13 | Head and arm motion
Simulated continuous head rotation and circular arm-tip paths. Original robot sound effects.

15
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:55,000
14 | Four-wheel motion
Simulated forward travel, broad moving arc, reverse and stop on a level floor.

16
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Assembly complete | Prototype design
Four motor screws or ties | Raised one-piece platform | Smaller arm boxes | Integrated fixed head mount | Physical tests required.
